.TITLE "uniq"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Filters or displays unique lines from a sorted file. it is used to __remove duplicates__ or count occurrences of repeated data in a text stream.

.DIV "TLDR"
**uniq file**
Removes consecutive duplicate lines and displays the unique lines.
> __file__ the target file

**uniq -c file**
Counts how many times each line occurs in the file.
> __-c__ count flag | __file__ the target file

**uniq -d file**
Displays only the lines that are duplicated in the file.
> __-d__ duplicates only flag

**uniq -u file**
Displays only the lines that are unique and do not have any duplicates.
> __-u__ unique only flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __uniq__ command only detects duplicate lines that are __adjacent__. therefore, you must almost always run __sort__ on your data before piping it into __uniq__ to ensure all duplicates are correctly identified.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:sort** **cli:grep** **cli:comm**

